{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"21 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,17.994,3.651,3.268,"HDFC Bank"],[13.889,14.731,36.509,2.373,2.124,"Retail loan growth and margin recovery"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"HDFC Bank reported Q2 FY27 standalone net profit of ₹19,510 cr, up 5% year"],[13.889,22.289,52.951,1.809,1.634,"on year; the shares have gained 16% since the 17-Oct-26 results (NIFTY: 11%)."],[13.889,23.733,52.936,1.809,1.634,"Net interest income rose 10% to ₹34,620 cr and advances under management"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"grew 7% year on year. Operating profit rose 6% as costs grew only 6%, while"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"provisions were 0.13% of loans. The NIM held at 3.29% in FY27E as the loan"],[13.889,28.065,40.482,1.809,1.634,"mix shifts toward higher-yielding retail and business banking."],[13.889,30.551,52.931,1.809,1.634,"1) Margin stability: the cost-of-funds advantage from a 34% CASA ratio and the"],[13.889,31.995,52.931,1.809,1.634,"repo-linked loan book keep the NIM near 3.3%; we take it from 3.29% in"],[13.889,33.439,52.934,1.809,1.634,"FY27E to 3.25% in FY28E, with NII growing 9% and 11%. 2) Provisions"],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"normalise from a trough: we carry loan-loss provisions at 0.40% of loans in"],[13.889,36.328,52.966,1.809,1.634,"FY28E from 0.24% in H1 FY27, as expected-credit-loss rules begin on 1 April"],[13.889,37.772,52.934,1.809,1.634,"2027. 3) EPS before one-offs grows 46%, 8% and 10% in FY27E-29E on our"],[13.889,39.216,30.096,1.809,1.634,"numbers, close to consensus of 53.0 and 61.3."],[13.889,41.702,52.966,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹1,040 averages two methods. A sum of parts gives ₹679:"],[13.889,43.146,52.964,1.809,1.634,"the bank at 1.36x Dec-27 book (₹525), on a 12% cost of equity and a 13% long-"],[13.889,44.59,52.959,1.809,1.634,"run return on book, plus subsidiaries at market value less 20% (₹154). HDFC"],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Bank's three-year average P/E of 17.0x gives ₹1,400. At ₹846 the shares assume"],[13.889,47.502,52.954,1.809,1.634,"a 15.1% long-run return; the bank guides to about 1.8% on assets and 13-15%"],[13.889,48.946,52.931,1.809,1.634,"on equity. Consensus is ₹962; 38 of 40 brokers say buy. We turn positive if core"],[13.889,50.39,52.966,1.809,1.634,"RoE holds above 15% under the new provisioning rules (target ₹1,080). Risks:"],[13.889,51.834,52.964,1.809,1.634,"unsecured retail loan stress, a sharper-than-expected NIM decline, and any RBI"],[13.889,53.278,14.839,1.809,1.634,"action on risk weights."],[13.889,55.766,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,64.377,1.489,1.022,0.915,"600"],[15.268,62.609,1.489,1.022,0.915,"700"],[15.268,60.842,1.489,1.022,0.915,"800"],[15.268,59.074,1.489,1.022,0.915,"900"],[14.451,57.307,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,000"],[17.913,65.071,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.539,65.071,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.326,65.071,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.08,65.071,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.438,66.242,3.643,1.275,1.111,"HDFCB ("],[22.084,66.268,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.697,66.242,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.781,66.242,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.721,67.403,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.559,67.403,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[29.845,67.403,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,67.403,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,68.468,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.22,68.468,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−13.2%"],[24.088,68.468,2.811,1.387,1.209,"18.8%"],[28.374,68.468,2.811,1.387,1.209,"16.7%"],[32.945,68.468,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−14.8%"],[15.492,69.533,1.476,1.387,1.209,"Rel"],[19.22,69.533,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−12.0%"],[24.64,69.533,2.26,1.387,1.209,"6.1%"],[28.374,69.533,2.811,1.387,1.209,"10.2%"],[32.945,69.533,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−13.3%"],[13.889,71.391,15.839,1.643,1.471,"Valuation (₹ per share)"],[13.889,72